      "name": "log_pdf_and_inverse_cdf_rho0.5_nu5",
      "note": "LogPDF at an interior point, and the conditional InverseCDF pair. C# InverseCDF(u, v) returns [u, v'] -- element 0 is the FIRST argument passed straight back (see ArchimedeanCopula.cs / NormalCopula.cs), so it is element 1, the conditionally inverted second variate, that carries the copula. Element 0 is asserted anyway to pin that pass-through contract, which the GenerateRandomValues sampling path depends on. Same theta as the pdf/cdf cases above.",
